from pathlib import Path
from docx import Document

src = Path(__file__).with_name("GENOVA_Studio_Software_Paper_Working_Draft.docx")
out = Path(__file__).with_name("GENOVA_Studio_Software_Paper_Working_Draft_v2.docx")
doc = Document(src)

replacements = {
5: "Current conclusion  GENOVA Studio is an Apple Silicon macOS research application with three integrated analytic pathways. It preserves the established jGENOVA core for supported balanced designs and adds bounded new Java implementations for unbalanced and multivariate analyses. Its contribution combines those new analytic capabilities with a GUI-first workflow, explicit design validation, typed outputs, reproducible exports, and visual D-study exploration.",
10: "Generalizability theory (G theory) studies the contribution of multiple measurement facets to score variation and supports decisions about alternative measurement designs. Established programs in the GENOVA family implement important analyses, but their input conventions and output formats can make routine work difficult for users who begin with tabular data. GENOVA Studio is an Apple Silicon macOS application that imports long-format tables, guides the user through design specification, validates the resulting design, presents analysis results in structured views, and exports machine-readable tables and reports. For complete balanced univariate designs, it invokes the original jGENOVA Java statistical core without changing its estimation code. In addition, GENOVA Studio introduces separate Java implementations for six unbalanced G-study designs and two multivariate G/D-study designs derived from published manuals and formulas. These newer pathways are deliberately bounded and labeled as pilots because their present validation evidence is design-specific, not because they are peripheral to the software. Regression tests compare the balanced pathway with the supplied jGENOVA output and compare the unbalanced and multivariate pathways with printed manual examples, independent calculations, synthetic cases, and structural rejection tests. A D-study grid, heatmap, and rotatable surface display exact engine results at calculated design points. This paper describes the software architecture, the three analytic pathways, supported designs, an illustrative workflow, validation evidence, and the boundaries of the current preview.",
16: "GENOVA Studio addresses this workflow as an Apple Silicon macOS application. It connects tabular import, explicit design choices, validation, analysis, export, and D-study visualization in one desktop interface. The statistical provenance of each pathway is visible to the user. The balanced GENOVA pathway uses the existing jGENOVA Java engine by Crick and Brennan. The urGENOVA and mGENOVA pathways are substantive new Java implementations based on published program manuals and formulas. They extend the application beyond a graphical wrapper by adding unbalanced and multivariate analyses that are not supplied by the jGENOVA source used in the balanced pathway. Their pilot designation describes the current breadth of supported designs and validation evidence; it does not reduce their role in the software architecture. The software does not present these implementations as the original urGENOVA or mGENOVA programs or as coverage of every design in those families.",
17: "The contribution is therefore both methodological and infrastructural. GENOVA Studio preserves an established statistical core where source code is available, implements bounded unbalanced and multivariate G-theory pathways where an equivalent open Java core was not available, exposes design assumptions before execution, prevents unsupported configurations, and makes outputs easier to audit and reuse. The paper does not claim a new general estimator, but it does claim an integrated, inspectable implementation of specific additional designs and their connection to a native macOS research workflow.",
46: "The current local validation record reports 416 automated checks. These cover all three analytic pathways, import and design rejection cases, Excel export types, the D-study grid and PNG surface, six urGENOVA pilot designs, two mGENOVA pilot designs, independent ANOVA cases, and locale behavior. The record also reports equality of the balanced official full report except for date and newline differences, successful execution with the bundled Java runtime, and unchanged hashes for 95 files in the original downloaded distributions. The validation script and machine-readable result record are retained with the project.",
50: "For urGENOVA, selected ANOVA terms and variance components reproduce the displayed precision of manual Appendices A, D, E, F, G, and H; a balanced Appendix C example is cross-checked against jGENOVA. For mGENOVA, the two supported models are compared with manual Appendices B, C, and D, including selected alternative D-study counts and unequal-weight examples. Independent synthetic cases, row-order permutations, and invalid-input tests add checks that are not merely copies of the printed examples. Together, these results provide affirmative evidence for the implemented configurations. Direct execution of the historical Windows programs could add another black-box comparison layer if those executables and suitable reference cases become available, but it is not a platform target or a prerequisite for the present Apple Silicon application claim.",
59: "The combination of configuration and explicit refusal is part of the intended impact. A useful statistical interface should make valid work easier while preventing unsupported work from looking routine. GENOVA Studio therefore reports why an imported structure cannot be analyzed under a selected family. It distinguishes the extensively validated balanced pathway from bounded urGENOVA and mGENOVA pathways while presenting all three as intentional components of the application.",
61: "The present application is a local Apple Silicon macOS preview. Public release still requires signing, notarization, documented installation, and release-level validation. Balanced analyses require complete designs within the stated jGENOVA scope. The urGENOVA pathway currently covers six restricted G-study structures and does not yet implement unbalanced D-study coefficients. The mGENOVA pathway currently covers two complete-cell multivariate random-effects structures; other canonical structures and general weighting matrices are outside the present implementation. Validation of the new engines is based on published manual examples, independent calculations, synthetic cases, invariance tests, and invalid-input tests. These sources provide meaningful evidence for the named configurations but do not establish correctness for every design or input permitted by the historical programs.",
64: "The first priority is release integrity rather than another platform build: resolve the license and attribution of each component, create a public versioned repository, run the validation suite against the immutable release, archive that release with a persistent identifier, provide one documented command that reproduces the checks, and sign and notarize the Apple Silicon macOS application. These steps strengthen distribution and reproducibility without changing the statistical claims.",
65: "The next statistical priority is to deepen validation within each implemented urGENOVA and mGENOVA design through a ladder of documented and systematically varied inputs, boundary cases, independent calculations, and external replication. Black-box comparison with historical executables would be useful supplementary evidence if a reliable execution environment and reference corpus are available, but it is not the definition of product maturity. Additional unbalanced D-study functions and mGENOVA structures should be added only after their inputs, covariance components, D-study rules, and reference outputs are defined. Unsupported designs should continue to be rejected explicitly during this expansion.",
68: "GENOVA Studio is an Apple Silicon macOS application that integrates data import, visual design configuration, explicit validation, analysis, structured results, export, and D-study exploration for a bounded set of G-theory applications. Its balanced pathway preserves the original jGENOVA computation. Its unbalanced and multivariate pathways are substantive new, separately implemented contributions whose current pilot status reflects limited design coverage and design-specific validation evidence. The next priorities are release-level reproducibility, deeper validation and independent replication of those new pathways, implementation of unbalanced D-study functionality, and carefully justified extension to additional multivariate designs."
}

for index, text in replacements.items():
    if index >= len(doc.paragraphs):
        raise IndexError(index)
    p = doc.paragraphs[index]
    p.text = text
    p.style = doc.paragraphs[index].style

doc.core_properties.title = "GENOVA Studio Software Paper Working Draft"
doc.core_properties.subject = "Apple Silicon macOS software paper with balanced unbalanced and multivariate G theory pathways"
doc.save(out)
print(out)
